+# Veterinarian Search Stays Out, Directory Filtering Comes In
+
+**Status:** Accepted
+
+## Context
+
+NG-9 declined searching for a pet, a visit, or a veterinarian, leaving owners as the only searchable records. The row was derived from observed absence during the 2026-07-31 bootstrap survey, so its provenance stayed open.
+
+A request on 2026-10-25 asked to narrow the veterinarian directory to one specialty. Read against the row as written, that request falls inside a declined capability. The owner decided the row at intake: "free-text veterinarian search stays out of scope, but filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in."
+
+## Options Considered
+
+1. **Keep NG-9 whole.** Decline the filter as veterinarian search. Rejected by the owner's decision.
+2. **Drop the veterinarian clause from NG-9.** Rejected: the owner kept free-text veterinarian search out of scope.
+3. **Narrow NG-9** (chosen). Free-text veterinarian search stays declined; filtering the directory by an attribute it already shows is in scope.
+
+## Decision
+
+NG-9 is narrowed. Free-text veterinarian search remains a non-goal. Filtering the veterinarian directory by an attribute it already shows, such as a specialty, is in scope. Pet and visit search remain declined, and their provenance stays part of the open consultation.
+
+## Consequences
+
+- The directory can be narrowed to one specialty on the page and on the machine-readable list.
+- A request for free-text veterinarian search, matching on names or partial text, still falls under NG-9.
+- A request to filter by an attribute the directory does not show is not covered by this narrowing.
+
+## Implementation
+
+**Non-goal:** NG-9
+
+- [PRD Non-Goals](../prd.md#non-goals) — the narrowed row and the updated preamble.
+- [PRD Veterinarian directory](../prd.md#req-vet-003) — the filter the narrowing admits.
